  "question": {
    "text": "At $25^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, the ionic product of water is $10^{-14}$. The free energy change for the self-ionization of water in $\\mathrm{kCal}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ is close to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "20.5",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "14.0",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "19.1",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "25.3",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\ell) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{H}^{+}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{OH}^{-}(\\mathrm{aq}) \\quad \\mathrm{K}=10^{-14}$\n$\\begin{aligned} \\Delta G^{\\circ} & =-2.303 \\mathrm{RT} \\text { logK } \\\\ & =-2.303 \\times 1.987 \\times 298 \\log 10^{-14} \\\\ & =2.303 \\times 1.987 \\times 298 \\times 14 \\\\ & =19091 \\mathrm{Cal} \\\\ & \\approx 19.1 \\mathrm{KCal}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
